HCF / GCD – Full Theory
1. What is HCF / GCD?

HCF → Highest Common Factor

GCD → Greatest Common Divisor
💬 Dono same hota hai, bas naam alag hai. HCF/GCD matlab woh “sabse bada factor” jo dono numbers ko divide kare.

Example:
12 and 18 → HCF = 6
💬 12 aur 18 ko divide karne wale numbers me sabse bada 6 hai, isiliye HCF 6.

2. Methods to Find HCF
METHOD 1: Factor Method

💬 Chhota method hai, par bade numbers me time lagta hai.

Example: HCF(12,18)
Factors of 12 → 1,2,3,4,6,12
Factors of 18 → 1,2,3,6,9,18
Common → 1,2,3,6
→ HCF = 6

💬 Bas common factors me sabse bada number hi HCF hota.

METHOD 2: Prime Factorization

💬 Ye method maths exam me best hota hai. Har number ko prime factors me todte hain.

24 = 2³ × 3
36 = 2² × 3²

Common: 2² × 3 = 12

💬 Common prime factors ki minimum powers lete hain, isiliye 2², 3¹.

METHOD 3: Euclid’s Algorithm (Fastest)

💬 Coding me sabse important method yahi hota. Very fast.

Formula:
HCF(a, b) = HCF(b, a % b)

Example: HCF(42, 30)
42 % 30 = 12
30 % 12 = 6
12 % 6 = 0
→ HCF = 6

💬 Jab remainder 0 ho jaata hai, jo last non-zero remainder hota hai woh HCF.

3. Properties of HCF

HCF(a,0) = a
💬 Koi bhi number 0 ke sath hoga toh HCF woh same number hota.

HCF(0,b) = b

HCF(a,b) ≤ min(a,b)
💬 HCF kabhi bhi numbers se bada nahi hota.

If a divides b → HCF = a
💬 Agar ek number dusre ka multiple ho toh chhota hi HCF.

HCF × LCM = Product of numbers
💬 Very important formula (exam favourite).

Example:
12 × 18 = 216
HCF = 6 → LCM = 216 / 6 = 36

4. HCF of 3 Numbers

Example: HCF(24,36,60)
HCF(24,36)=12
HCF(12,60)=12

💬 Step-by-step karna hota hai. Pehle do ka HCF, phir tisre ke sath.

5. Shortcut Tricks

Consecutive numbers → HCF = 1
💬 Reason: Unke beech koi common factor nahi hota.

Both prime → HCF = 1
💬 Prime numbers ka koi common factor 1 ke alawa nahi hota.

If one divides the other → HCF = smaller number
💬 Jaise 15 aur 45 ka HCF = 15.

6. Example Problems

HCF(8,20)=4

HCF(27,36)=9

HCF(48,180)=12

💬 Har example alag method se solve ho sakta, iss se confidence badhta.